'<!-- Section properties of a solid ellipse: area, $I_x = \tfrac{\pi}{4} a b^3$, $I_y = \tfrac{\pi}{4} a^3 b$, section moduli and radii of gyration. -->
"Geometrical Properties of Ellipse
'<div style="max-width:120mm"><img style="height:112pt;" alt="ellipse.png" class="side" src="../../Images/mechanics/sections/ellipse.png"></div>
'Dimensions
a=? {2}'m,'b=? {1}'m
'Area
A = π*a*b'm<sup>2</sup>
'Centroid
y_c = a'm,'z_c = b'm
'Perimeter (approx.)
P = π*(3*(a+b)-sqr((3*a+b)*(a+3*b)))'m
'Second moments of area
I_y = π*a*b^3/4'm<sup>4</sup>
I_z = π*b*a^3/4'm<sup>4</sup>
'Polar moment of area
I_x = I_y + I_z'm<sup>4</sup>
'Torsional constant
I_t = π*a^3*b^3/(a^2 + b^2)'m<sup>4</sup>
'Torsional section modulus
#if '<!--'b < a'-->
a'&gt;'b
W_t = π*a*b^2/2'm<sup>3</sup>
#else
a'&lt;'b
W_t = π*b*a^2/2'm<sup>3</sup>
#end if
'Radii of gyration
r_y = sqrt(I_y/A)'m
r_z = sqrt(I_z/A)'m
r_x = sqrt(I_x/A)'m
